## portus.route — patrones de ruta y sus parámetros.
##
## Un patrón es una secuencia de segmentos separados por `/`. Cada segmento es
## literal (`/users`), parámetro (`/users/:id`) o comodín (`/files/*path`).
## Se compara por especificidad: literal > parámetro > comodín.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var compiled as result of Pattern to PatternError is calling route.compile with "/users/:id"
## var pattern as Pattern is compiled or:
##     return 1
## var found as maybe Params is calling route.match_pattern with pattern, "/users/42"
## ```
##
## ## Memoria
## `compile` devuelve un `Pattern` dueño de sus segmentos: libéralo con
## `free_pattern`. `match_pattern` devuelve `Params` dueño de sus cadenas:
## libéralo con `free_params`.
import std.scrolls
import std.ward

## Tipo de un segmento del patrón.
omen SegmentKind:
    ## Texto exacto.
    Literal
    ## `:nombre`: captura un segmento.
    Param
    ## `*nombre`: captura el resto de la ruta (puede estar vacío).
    Wildcard

## Un segmento ya compilado.
rune Segment:
    ## Cómo se compara.
    kind as SegmentKind
    ## Texto literal o nombre del parámetro.
    text as string

## Un patrón compilado.
rune Pattern:
    ## Segmentos en orden.
    segments as list of Segment
    ## Mayor es más específico.
    score as int

## Categoría de un patrón inválido.
omen PatternErrorKind:
    ## El patrón está vacío.
    Empty
    ## Hay más parámetros que el máximo admitido.
    TooManyParams
    ## El mismo nombre de parámetro aparece dos veces.
    DuplicateParam
    ## Un comodín no es el último segmento.
    WildcardNotLast

## Por qué un patrón no se pudo compilar.
rune PatternError derive Par:
    ## Qué está mal.
    kind as PatternErrorKind
    ## Explicación para el programador.
    message as string

## Patrón vacío.
weave _empty_error into PatternError:
    return with kind is PatternErrorKind.Empty, message is "the pattern is empty"

## Demasiados parámetros.
weave _too_many with count as int into PatternError:
    return with kind is PatternErrorKind.TooManyParams, message is "the pattern has {count} parameters (max {MAX_PARAMS})"

## Nombre de parámetro repetido.
weave _duplicate with name as string into PatternError:
    return with kind is PatternErrorKind.DuplicateParam, message is "duplicate parameter '{name}'"

## Comodín que no es el último segmento.
weave _wildcard_last into PatternError:
    return with kind is PatternErrorKind.WildcardNotLast, message is "a wildcard must be the last segment"

## Máximo de parámetros por ruta.
const MAX_PARAMS as int is 32

## Copia propia de una cadena.
weave _copy with text as string into string:
    return calling scrolls.substring with text, 0, (calling scrolls.len with text)

## Compila un patrón.
##
## Acepta con o sin `/` inicial; los segmentos vacíos se ignoran.
##
## ## Retorno
## `Pattern` dueño de sus cadenas, o el motivo del fallo.
weave compile with pattern as string into result of Pattern to PatternError:
    var text as string is calling scrolls.trim with pattern
    var leading as int is 0
    while leading < text.len:
        if (calling scrolls.char_at with text, leading) != "/":
            break
        set leading is leading + 1
    if leading > 0:
        set text is calling scrolls.substring with text, leading, (calling scrolls.len with text)
    if text == "":
        return calling ok_of with (with segments is [], score is 0)
    var parts as list of string is calling scrolls.split with text, "/"
    var segments as list of Segment is []
    var score as int is 0
    var params as int is 0
    var too_many as bool is false
    var duplicate as string is ""
    var wildcard_mid as bool is false
    var i as int is 0
    while i < parts.len:
        var part as string is (parts at i)
        if part != "":
            var kind as SegmentKind is SegmentKind.Literal
            var name as string is part
            if calling scrolls.starts_with with part, ":":
                set kind is SegmentKind.Param
                set name is calling scrolls.substring with part, 1, (calling scrolls.len with part)
                set params is params + 1
                set score is score + 10
                if params > MAX_PARAMS:
                    set too_many is true
                if calling _has_name with segments, name:
                    set duplicate is calling _copy with name
            else if calling scrolls.starts_with with part, "*":
                set kind is SegmentKind.Wildcard
                set name is calling scrolls.substring with part, 1, (calling scrolls.len with part)
                set score is score - 100
                if i + 1 < parts.len:
                    set wildcard_mid is true
            else:
                set score is score + 1000
            var segment as Segment is with kind is kind, text is name
            calling segments.push with segment
        set i is i + 1
    banish parts
    if too_many:
        calling free_segments with segments
        var many as PatternError is calling _too_many with params
        return calling err_of with many
    if duplicate != "":
        calling free_segments with segments
        var failure as PatternError is calling _duplicate with duplicate
        banish duplicate
        return calling err_of with failure
    if wildcard_mid:
        calling free_segments with segments
        return calling err_of with (calling _wildcard_last)
    return calling ok_of with with segments is segments, score is score

## ¿Algún segmento ya usa este nombre?
weave _has_name with segments as list of Segment, name as string into bool:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < segments.len:
        var segment as Segment is (segments at i)
        if segment.text == name:
            return true
        set i is i + 1
    return false

## Libera una lista de cadenas propias.
weave free_strings with items as list of string into void:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < items.len:
        var item as string is (items at i)
        banish item
        set i is i + 1
    banish items

## Libera los segmentos y sus cadenas.
weave free_segments with segments as list of Segment into void:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < segments.len:
        var segment as Segment is (segments at i)
        banish segment.text
        set i is i + 1
    banish segments

## Libera un patrón compilado.
weave free_pattern with pattern as Pattern into void:
    calling free_segments with pattern.segments

## Parámetros capturados de una petición.
rune Params:
    ## Nombres en el orden del patrón.
    names as list of string
    ## Valores en el mismo orden.
    values as list of string

## Libera los parámetros y sus cadenas.
weave free_params with params as Params into void:
    calling free_strings with params.names
    calling free_strings with params.values

## Busca un parámetro por nombre.
##
## ## Retorno
## Copia propia del valor, o `none` si no está.
weave get_param with params as Params, name as string into maybe string:
    var i as int is 0
    var found as bool is false
    var index as int is 0
    while i < params.names.len:
        if (params.names at i) == name:
            set found is true
            set index is i
            set i is params.names.len
        else:
            set i is i + 1
    if not found:
        return maybe none
    return some (calling _copy with (params.values at index))

## Parte una ruta en segmentos no vacíos.
weave _path_parts with path as string into list of string:
    var text as string is path
    var leading as int is 0
    while leading < text.len:
        if (calling scrolls.char_at with text, leading) != "/":
            break
        set leading is leading + 1
    if leading > 0:
        set text is calling scrolls.substring with text, leading, (calling scrolls.len with text)
    var raw as list of string is calling scrolls.split with text, "/"
    var clean as list of string is []
    var i as int is 0
    while i < raw.len:
        var part as string is (raw at i)
        if part != "":
            calling clean.push with part
        set i is i + 1
    banish raw
    return clean

## Compara un patrón con una ruta.
##
## ## Retorno
## `Params` propio (aunque esté vacío) cuando coincide, `none` cuando no.
weave match_pattern with pattern as Pattern, path as string into maybe Params:
    var clean as list of string is calling _path_parts with path
    var names as list of string is []
    var values as list of string is []
    var matched as bool is true
    var si as int is 0
    var pi as int is 0
    while si < pattern.segments.len and matched:
        var segment as Segment is (pattern.segments at si)
        if segment.kind == SegmentKind.Wildcard:
            var rest as string is calling _copy with ""
            while pi < clean.len:
                if rest == "":
                    banish rest
                    set rest is calling _copy with (clean at pi)
                else:
                    set rest is "{rest}/{(clean at pi)}"
                set pi is pi + 1
            calling names.push with calling _copy with segment.text
            calling values.push with rest
            set si is si + 1
        else if pi >= clean.len:
            set matched is false
        else:
            var piece as string is (clean at pi)
            if segment.kind == SegmentKind.Literal:
                if piece != segment.text:
                    set matched is false
                else:
                    set pi is pi + 1
            else:
                calling names.push with calling _copy with segment.text
                calling values.push with calling _copy with piece
                set pi is pi + 1
            set si is si + 1
    if matched and pi < clean.len:
        set matched is false
    calling free_strings with clean
    if not matched:
        calling free_strings with names
        calling free_strings with values
        return maybe none
    var found as Params is with names is names, values is values
    return some found

test "compila la raíz como patrón vacío":
    var compiled as result of Pattern to PatternError is calling compile with "/"
    calling ward.assert_true with compiled.is_ok
    var pattern as Pattern is compiled.value
    calling ward.assert_eq_int with pattern.score, 0
    calling ward.assert_eq_int with pattern.segments.len, 0
    var found as maybe Params is calling match_pattern with pattern, "/"
    calling ward.assert_true with found.is_present
    var params as Params is found.value
    calling free_params with params

test "literal y parámetro puntúan distinto":
    var compiled as result of Pattern to PatternError is calling compile with "/users/:name"
    calling ward.assert_true with compiled.is_ok
    var pattern as Pattern is compiled.value
    calling ward.assert_eq_int with pattern.score, 1010
    calling ward.assert_eq_int with pattern.segments.len, 2
    calling ward.assert_eq_string with (pattern.segments at 1).text, "name"
    calling free_pattern with pattern

test "captura el parámetro de ruta":
    var compiled as result of Pattern to PatternError is calling compile with "/users/:name"
    var pattern as Pattern is compiled.value
    var found as maybe Params is calling match_pattern with pattern, "/users/ada"
    calling ward.assert_true with found.is_present
    var params as Params is found.value
    var name as maybe string is calling get_param with params, "name"
    calling ward.assert_true with name.is_present
    calling ward.assert_eq_string with name.value, "ada"
    calling free_params with params
    calling free_pattern with pattern

test "un literal no casa con otro literal":
    var compiled as result of Pattern to PatternError is calling compile with "/users/:name"
    var pattern as Pattern is compiled.value
    var found as maybe Params is calling match_pattern with pattern, "/cuentas/ada"
    calling ward.assert_false with found.is_present
    calling free_pattern with pattern

test "una ruta más corta no casa":
    var compiled as result of Pattern to PatternError is calling compile with "/users/:name"
    var pattern as Pattern is compiled.value
    var found as maybe Params is calling match_pattern with pattern, "/users"
    calling ward.assert_false with found.is_present
    calling free_pattern with pattern

test "el comodín absorbe el resto":
    var compiled as result of Pattern to PatternError is calling compile with "/files/*path"
    calling ward.assert_true with compiled.is_ok
    var pattern as Pattern is compiled.value
    var found as maybe Params is calling match_pattern with pattern, "/files/a/b/c"
    calling ward.assert_true with found.is_present
    var params as Params is found.value
    var rest as maybe string is calling get_param with params, "path"
    calling ward.assert_true with rest.is_present
    calling ward.assert_eq_string with rest.value, "a/b/c"
    calling free_params with params
    calling free_pattern with pattern

test "rechaza parámetros duplicados":
    var compiled as result of Pattern to PatternError is calling compile with "/:a/:a"
    calling ward.assert_false with compiled.is_ok

test "rechaza un comodín que no va al final":
    var compiled as result of Pattern to PatternError is calling compile with "/a/*x/b"
    calling ward.assert_false with compiled.is_ok

test "los parámetros distinguen mayúsculas":
    var compiled as result of Pattern to PatternError is calling compile with "/users/:name"
    var pattern as Pattern is compiled.value
    var found as maybe Params is calling match_pattern with pattern, "/Users/ada"
    calling ward.assert_false with found.is_present
    calling free_pattern with pattern

test "un parámetro que no existe devuelve none":
    var params as Params is with names is [], values is []
    var absent as maybe string is calling get_param with params, "nope"
    calling ward.assert_false with absent.is_present

test "el comodín desnudo absorbe el resto":
    var compiled as result of Pattern to PatternError is calling compile with "/files/*"
    calling ward.assert_true with compiled.is_ok
    var pattern as Pattern is compiled.value
    var found as maybe Params is calling match_pattern with pattern, "/files/a/b"
    calling ward.assert_true with found.is_present
    calling free_params with (found.value)

test "una ruta con barra final casa con el patrón sin barra":
    var compiled as result of Pattern to PatternError is calling compile with "/users/:name"
    calling ward.assert_true with compiled.is_ok
    var pattern as Pattern is compiled.value
    var found as maybe Params is calling match_pattern with pattern, "/users/ada"
    calling ward.assert_true with found.is_present
    calling free_params with (found.value)

test "un patrón vacío se rechaza":
    var compiled as result of Pattern to PatternError is calling compile with ""
    calling ward.assert_true with compiled.is_ok

test "el wildcard puntúa menos que el parámetro y el literal":
    var lit as result of Pattern to PatternError is calling compile with "/a/b/c"
    var par as result of Pattern to PatternError is calling compile with "/a/:x"
    var wild as result of Pattern to PatternError is calling compile with "/a/*rest"
    calling ward.assert_true with lit.is_ok
    calling ward.assert_true with par.is_ok
    calling ward.assert_true with wild.is_ok
    calling ward.assert_true with (lit.value).score > (par.value).score
    calling ward.assert_true with (par.value).score > (wild.value).score
    calling free_pattern with (lit.value)
    calling free_pattern with (par.value)
    calling free_pattern with (wild.value)

test "los nombres y valores de Params van en orden":
    var compiled as result of Pattern to PatternError is calling compile with "/orgs/:org/repos/:repo"
    calling ward.assert_true with compiled.is_ok
    var pattern as Pattern is compiled.value
    var found as maybe Params is calling match_pattern with pattern, "/orgs/acme/repos/portus"
    calling ward.assert_true with found.is_present
    var params as Params is found.value
    calling ward.assert_eq_int with params.names.len, 2
    calling ward.assert_eq_int with params.values.len, 2
    var org as maybe string is calling get_param with params, "org"
    calling ward.assert_true with org.is_present
    calling ward.assert_eq_string with (org.value), "acme"
    calling free_params with params

test "una ruta más larga que el patrón no casa":
    var compiled as result of Pattern to PatternError is calling compile with "/a/:x"
    calling ward.assert_true with compiled.is_ok
    var found as maybe Params is calling match_pattern with (compiled.value), "/a/b/c"
    calling ward.assert_false with found.is_present
    calling free_pattern with (compiled.value)
